                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Toadled is deceptive - it's both surprisingly difficult, and surprisingly... disturbed. I didn't expect quite as much body-horror as I got from Toadled, not that it really bothered me all that much, but it was a welcome change of pace. Gameplay wise, it's exceedingly simple but speeds up remarkably fast (probably why the slowdown exists baseline and can be chained almost non-stop). Overall, though, I think just letting the slowdown be toggled on permanently by the end might've been a nice choice but it doesn't really matter since Toadled won't keep you playing long enough to get boring. Simple, decent fun, easily moved past.",
